#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:5
#: ee0c2667d8ec43a0b8c8f9ecce5afe0a
msgid "Frame Assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:7
#: c3fe0eefa03f4d349a25e6e797d5181d
msgid "Any servo based Pan & Tilt gimbal should work.  Ideally the system should allow 180 degrees of pan rotation in both directions and 90degrees of pitch both up and down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:11
#: 5c7a3708701e4b2dbba8cb397fc6f080
msgid "The servos used can either be regular servos that translate the PWM input into an absolute angle or continuous rotation servos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:15
#: 8f8b5b64041640a6bde73693b97a7d09
msgid "Recommended Frames"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:17
#: 7975046b8228471aa956e6ae7665bd3f
msgid "The following have been tested and shown to work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:19
#: b56776227cfd41b38615ec4404699052
msgid "`Eagle Eyes Antenna Tracker <http://www.readymaderc.com/store/index.php?main_page=product_info&cPath=11_27&products_id=96>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:21
#: 59b8d2ca57144c57a7848923210b96d8
msgid "These systems also likely work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:23
#: 01fe2f659b464597a8be72a729add338
msgid "`Servo City PT785-S Pan & Tilt System <http://www.servocity.com/html/pt785-s_pan___tilt_system.html#.U_BL3I8c038>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:26
#: 2067be43d89d45759c3d9da59fe25e51
msgid "Mounting the flight controller board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:31
#: 9a4f680e36fe4405988a884e1143622c
msgid "The flight controller board should be mounted on the moving part of the antenna tracker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:34
#: 27c9147e2d0d44f38bc931872cd95db3
msgid "If possible align the front of the flight controller so that it points exactly in the direction that the antenna is most sensitive.  So for example, if using a Pixhawk controller and a Yagi antenna, the arrow on the top of the Pixhawk should point in the same direction as the antenna."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:40
#: bb343ef70f4c47bd8e429542a857b01d
msgid "Alternatively the flight controller can be mounted at any 45deg or 90deg angle to the antenna and then the AHRS_ORIENTATION parameter can be changed to account for the difference.  :ref:`See the configuration page for more details <configuration_setting_the_ahrs_orientation>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:45
#: 605e6e1afe154b2b9f740ad773c44dfd
msgid "Connecting the servos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:50
#: 30e08262836442749fde63bd66ac9847
msgid "The Pan servo (controls the tracker's heading or yaw) should be connected to RC1, the Tilt servo (controls elevation or pitch) should be connected to RC2. A BEC or ESC should be connected to any of the other RC outputs as shown to provide power for the servos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:56
#: c96e136751154b8e8441dfc4f470bef1
msgid "Connecting the radio and antenna"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:61
#: efc2a59128db43eeb9d0a55a28c8fc07
msgid "The Antenna should be attached to the radio after first removing the radio's di-pole antenna.  Note that the 3DR and RFD900 radios have a RP SMA Male adapter (RP = reverse polarity) while antennas can come with a number of different connectors meaning an adapter (such as `this RP SMA Female to SMA Female adapter <http://www.readymaderc.com/store/index.php?main_page=product_info&cPath=11_45_58&products_id=432>`__) may be required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:68
#: cd34fc9d5feb4343bbd5d756397ee1a5
msgid "Mounting the GPS and external compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:70
#: 1992025e30bb42f5a5f13dd1e41f12ed
msgid "If using a GPS+compass module it should be mounted so that the arrow on the module points in the same direction as the antenna. If this is not convenient, the COMPASS_ORIENT parameter can be used to account for this. :ref:`See the configuration page for more details <configuration_setting_the_compass_orientation>`.  Care should be taken to ensure the compass is not close to any metal objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/frame-assembly.rst:76
#: b15238f2e04f4c3f95771344873711fa
msgid "If using a stand-alone GPS (i.e. not an integrated GPS+compass) the GPS should be positioned so that its antenna has a clear view of the sky. Its heading is not important. Some care should be taken to ensure the cable connected to the flight controller cannot become tangled."
msgstr ""
